       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nHere are some options within the limit:\n- **800 mg orally four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum.\n- **600 mg orally four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg orally four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), which is often enough for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIbuprofen is best taken with food, at the lowest effective dose, for the shortest time needed.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter it as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily. Tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it."
      }
